  "question": {
    "text": "If $k \\leq \\sin ^{-1} x+\\cos ^{-1} x+\\tan ^{-1} x \\leq K,$ then $-$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{k}=0, \\mathrm{~K}=\\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{k}=0, \\mathrm{~K}=\\pi / 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{k}=\\pi / 2, \\mathrm{~K}=\\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\sin ^{-1} x+\\cos ^{-1} x+\\tan ^{-1} x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\tan ^{-1} x$\r\nSince domain of the function $\\mathrm{x} \\in[-1,1]$ $\\therefore-\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\leq \\tan ^{-1} x \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\nHence, $\\mathrm{k}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ and $\\mathrm{K}=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}$"
  }
}